  "objectives": [
    "Identify the four heart chambers (RA, RV, LA, LV), four heart valves (tricuspid, pulmonary, mitral/bicuspid, aortic), and the major entering/leaving vessels (SVC, IVC, pulmonary arteries/veins, aorta).",
    "Trace blood flow through the heart in order to explain dual-loop circulation (pulmonary vs systemic).",
    "Explain why the right and left sides of the heart support different functions and pressure outputs.",
    "Relate ventricular wall thickness to the pressure/work required for systemic versus pulmonary circulation.",
    "Describe how atrioventricular and semilunar valves prevent backflow during cardiac cycle timing."
